@meta
id: 20-20
title: Scenario — the provider in shape
chapter: 20
type: scenario
skills: register-named, register-blackhole, register-expression, register-zero, op-to-mark, marks-set, dot-repeat
par: 140
minutes: 14
vscode: a calculator, a lot of Ctrl-X and Ctrl-V, and a reviewer who spots the debug line
open: order.provider.ts

@brief
A ticket, not an exercise.

    ORD-433  OrderProvider is out of shape.
             1. Methods in lifecycle order: findOne, cancel, settle.
             2. settle must refuse an order that is already SETTLED,
                the same way cancel refuses one that is SHIPPED. The
                code is ORDER_ALREADY_SETTLED. Replace the TODO.
             3. The debug line in cancel goes.
             4. REFUND_WINDOW_MS becomes a plain number. The build
                step cannot fold `30 * 86_400_000` in a decorator.

One file. Nothing in it is retyped that already exists: the `settle`
method moves whole, the guard is a copy of the one in `cancel` with two
words changed, and the number is computed, not looked up. Every line
that is not mentioned stays exactly as it is.

@keys
| `ma` then `"ad'a` | mark a line, delete from it to here into `a` |
| `"aP` | put the register above the cursor line |
| `"_dd` then `P` | delete into nothing, then the plain put still holds the yank |
| `Ctrl-R =` | compute inside insert mode |
| `cw` then `.` | change a word, repeat on the next match |

@hints
Do the number first: it is on line 6 and `ct;` changes everything up to
the semicolon. Type the multiplication into the expression register
instead of the answer.
--
`settle` is thirteen lines, blank line above included. Mark the blank
line, `/async find` Enter, `kk` to the method's closing brace, and
`"ad'a` takes the lot into `a`. `G"aP` puts it above the class's last
brace, blank line and all.
--
Yank the three-line guard from `cancel`, `"_dd` the TODO, `P`. The
put block still says `SHIPPED` twice: `/SHIPPED` Enter, `cwSETTLED`,
`n`, `.`.
--
`/debug` Enter, `"_dd`. Plain `dd` is fine here too; by this point
there is nothing left to put.

@solution
One route that measures 121 keystrokes.

**The number.** `/= 30` Enter, `w`, `ct;`, `Ctrl-R =30*86400000` Enter,
`Esc`. The literal `86_400_000` is not an expression vim understands,
so the underscores go.

**The move.** `/settle(` Enter, `k`, `ma`. `/async find` Enter, `kk`,
`"ad'a`. `G`, `"aP`. The register carries the blank line at the top of
the block, so the spacing is right at the destination and the blank
that was below `settle` closes the gap it left.

**The guard.** `/if (order` Enter — it wraps to `cancel`, the only
`if (order` left — `3yy`. `/TODO` Enter, `"_dd`, `P`. Then `/SHIPPED`
Enter, `cwSETTLED`, `Esc`, `n`, `.`.

**The debug line.** `/debug` Enter, `"_dd`. `:wq`.

Three registers did the work: `a` held a method across a jump to the
end of the file, `"_` kept the TODO out of the way of the guard you had
just yanked, and `=` did the multiplication. The unnamed register was
used once, on purpose, for the put right after the yank.

That is the shape of register use in real editing. Name the things you
must not lose. Throw away the things you do not want. Let the unnamed
register do everything that is yank-then-put with nothing in between.
Chapter 21 adds one more register to the list, `q`, and it changes what
the letters can hold from text to keystrokes.

@start order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

const REFUND_WINDOW_MS = 30 * 86_400_000;

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async settle(id: string, total: number) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    // TODO: same guard as cancel

    await this.paymentService.capture(order.id, total);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'SETTLED', total },
    });
  }

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);
    this.logger.debug('cancel', id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    if (Date.now() - order.placedAt.getTime() <= REFUND_WINDOW_MS) {
      await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);
    }

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}

@expected order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

const REFUND_WINDOW_MS = 2592000000;

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    if (Date.now() - order.placedAt.getTime() <= REFUND_WINDOW_MS) {
      await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);
    }

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }

  public async settle(id: string, total: number) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SETTLED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SETTLED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.capture(order.id, total);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'SETTLED', total },
    });
  }
}
